// ─── Where the journal comes from ───────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Sam types almost nothing. Each source is a command whose output Axiom reads:
// - a record that matches a flow already written (same account and amount,
//   within three days) is left alone;
// - one that keeps a contract is written as the occurrence (`01 flat`);
// - one from Halcyon that mentions INV-2026-01 settles that invoice;
// - the rest are written as flows with the party each memo names.
// `axiom sync --dry` shows what would be written. Nothing written is changed.

/// Chase's export of the checking account.
sync checking
  run   chase-export checking --since {since}
  csv   date "Posting Date" "MM/DD/YYYY", amount "Amount", memo "Description", balance "Balance"

/// The card's export shows charges as positive amounts.
sync visa
  run   chase-export visa --since {since}
  csv   date "Transaction Date" "MM/DD/YYYY", amount "Amount" flipped, memo "Description"

/// Quotes for everything held, by year.
sync prices
  run   quotes {units} --since {since}
  into  prices/{year}.ax

/// Invoice codes, as they appear in memos (`INV-2026-01`).
code inv-*
  on client

// How parties appear on statements is part of who they are: see `known-as` in
// parties.ax. A memo nobody is known as is written to `?`, and `check` offers
// the line that would recognize it.
